From de681dd0ad37f76f1d156f05ee405156903a02dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden PS4 <eden-ps4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:14:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 67/68] dynarmic: exclusive loads and stores inline through the
 page table; a locked no-op for DMB

Without fastmem, every exclusive load and store (LDREX/STREX, LDXR/STXR and their sizes) was a
call into the global monitor and the memory callbacks, its lock taken even with
Unsafe_IgnoreGlobalMonitor (which only the inline fastmem path honoured). They now go inline
through the page table walk, as the fastmem path does through fastmem: the monitor's address and
value stored, the load read through the walk, the store a lock cmpxchg against the value loaded.
An access the walk can't do (unmapped, across a page, a store to a marked page) takes the same
fallbacks the fastmem path uses. 128-bit exclusives keep the monitor path.
(UserConfig::page_table_inline_exclusives, on by default; with a page table and without fastmem.)

DMB was an mfence; a locked OR of zero into the stack's top is as strong a barrier for ordinary
memory, and about half the cost (as Linux's smp_mb on x86-64). DSB keeps mfence and lfence.

Host harness (A32 and A64, Eden's page table configuration): an atomic increment and decrement
with barriers 316-423 ns -> 79-98 ns (A32), 360-450 -> 53-68 ns (A64); random programs of
exclusives on ordinary, marked and unmapped pages give the same registers and memory both ways
(A32: 2800, A64: 1040).
